termediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, SEIICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKIGUCHI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YATSUI, TOKUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMIYA YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO SEIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKIGUCHI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YATSUI TOKUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMIYA, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, SEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKIGUCHI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YATSUI, TOKUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electrically operated valve capable of preventing noise from occurring at the time of impact by reducing the number of parts without providing a stopper to stop the rotation of a rotor at the time of full opening and full closing of a valve disc, comprising a shaft (18) which is fixed to a rotor (17) and has male threads (20), the valve disc (6) which has a needle valve (5) on one end part, forms female threads (16) screwed onto the male threads (20) on the other end part, and has a connection part (14) which connects the needle valve (5) to the female threads (16), and a valve body (1) having a guide part which stops the rotation of the valve disc (6) and guides it reciprocatingly in axial direction, wherein an upper end part of the shaft (18) is supported by a supporting part provided on the top wall side of a case (22), and the lower end part is supported rotatably by a bearing member (13) fixed to the valve disc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une soupape à commande électrique capable d'empêcher l'émission d'un bruit au moment de l'impact, grâce à un nombre réduit de pièces, sans l'intervention d'un organe d'arrêt destiné à arrêter la rotation d'un rotor lors de l'ouverture totale et de la fermeture totale d'un disque de soupape. La soupape selon l'invention comprend un arbre (18) fixé à un rotor (17) et comportant des filetages mâles (20), le disque (6) de soupape, qui comprend une soupape à pointeau (5) à une extrémité, formant des filetages femelles (16) s'engageant sur les filetages mâles (20) à l'autre extrémité et comportant un segment (14) de raccordement qui relie la soupape à pointeau (5) aux filetages femelles (16) ; et un corps (1) de soupape comportant une partie de guidage qui arrête la rotation du disque (6) de soupape et l'entraîne dans un mouvement alternatif dans la direction axiale, une extrémité supérieure de l'arbre (18) étant disposée sur un segment de support se trouvant sur la paroi supérieure d'un carter (22) et l'extrémité inférieure étant disposée rotative sur un élément d'appui (13) fixé au disque (6) de soupape.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set 